Files of this directory that end in .toml are read, in file name order, after
/etc/emfor/emfor.toml (include_dir). Use 01-, 10-, 99- as prefixes; a later
file overrides an earlier one. This file is not read.

The directory and the files must be owned by root (or by the user emfor runs
as) and not writable by group or others, or emfor refuses the config. A service
looks like this:

  [services."api.svc.emfor"]
  check = "tcp"
  backends = ["10.0.0.11:8080", "10.0.0.12:8080"]

Check with `emfor check-config`, apply with `systemctl reload emfor`.
Manual: /usr/share/doc/emfor/ (chapter 5, "Configuring emfor").
